/*!
\page page_stetofhit StETofHit

\brief Reconstructed hit in the STAR Endcap Time-of-Flight (eTOF) detector.

\section etofhit_overview Overview

StETofHit represents a fully reconstructed hit in the STAR Endcap TOF (eTOF) detector,
introduced for the BES-II programme in Run 19 (2019).
The eTOF covers 1.4 < |η| < 1.7 on the west endcap using MRPC technology.

An eTOF hit is formed by merging two \ref StETofDigi objects from opposite ends (sides) of
the same MRPC strip.
- The hit time is the calibrated average of the two digi times.
- The local Y position along the strip is determined from the time difference between the two ends.
- The cluster size records how many strips contributed.

Geometry: 3 sectors (STAR sectors 7–9) × 3 z-planes × 3 counters = 27 MRPC modules,
each with 32 strips.

Hits are stored in \ref StETofCollection via StEvent::etofCollection().

\section etofhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
TObject → StObject → StETofHit
\endcode

\section etofhit_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| mSector | UInt_t | STAR sector number (e.g., 7, 8, 9) |
| mZPlane | UInt_t | z-plane number within sector (1–3) |
| mCounter | UInt_t | Counter (MRPC module) number (1–3) |
| mTime | Double_t | Calibrated hit time [ns] |
| mTotalTot | Double_t | Summed time-over-threshold from both digis [ns] |
| mClusterSize | UInt_t | Number of contributing strips |
| mLocalX | Double_t | Local X position on counter [cm] |
| mLocalY | Double_t | Local Y position from timing difference [cm] |
| mAssociatedTrack | StTrack* | Matched reconstructed track |
| mIdTruth | UShort_t | MC truth track ID |
| mQuality | UShort_t | MC truth quality (% charge from truth) |

\section etofhit_methods Key Methods

- sector() — STAR sector number
- zPlane() — z-plane number (1–3)
- counter() — counter (MRPC) number (1–3)
- time() — calibrated hit time [ns]
- totalTot() — summed time-over-threshold [ns]
- clusterSize() — strip cluster multiplicity
- localX(), localY() — local position on counter face [cm]
- associatedTrack() — pointer to matched StTrack
- idTruth(), qaTruth() — MC truth information
- operator<, compare() — sort/compare by time
- setHwAddress(sector, zPlane, counter) — set geometry in one call

\section etofhit_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StETofCollection* coll = event->etofCollection();
if (coll) {
    const StSPtrVecETofHit& hits = coll->etofHits();
    for (const auto& h : hits) {
        unsigned int sector  = h->sector();
        unsigned int zPlane  = h->zPlane();
        unsigned int counter = h->counter();
        double       time    = h->time();
        double       tot     = h->totalTot();
        double       localY  = h->localY(); // position from timing difference
    }
}
\endcode

\see StETofDigi, StETofHeader, StETofCollection
*/
